<title>GERMANY: Kohl insists on punctual start for currency union.</title>
<headline>Kohl insists on punctual start for currency union.</headline>
<byline>Clifford Coonan</byline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Chancellor Helmut Kohl said in a newspaper report on Sunday that it was of vital importance that European Economic and Monetary Union start punctually on January 1, 1999.</p>
<p>However, German Finance Minister Theo Waigel said elsewhere that strict fulfillment of the Maastricht criteria must take precedence over the scheduled start of the EU single currency.</p>
</text>
